                <head>152. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 13, 1964, Secretary of State Rusk,
                    accompanied by Under Secretary Ball,
                    testified on East-West trade before the Senate Foreign Relations Committee. A
                    detailed draft outline of the Secretary’s testimony, prepared in S/P on March 3, is attached to a March 3 memorandum
                    from Edward Fried to
                        Springsteen. (Department of State, S/PC Files: Lot 70 D
                    199, Economic Policy—1964) The transcript of his prepared statement (Department
                    of State Press Release No. 108, March 13) is ibid. Rusk and Ball’s entire
                    testimony was subsequently published in <hi rendition="#italic">East-West Trade:
                        Hearings Before the Committee on Foreign Relations, United States Senate,
                        Eighty-eighth Congress, Second Session</hi> (Washington: Government Printing
                    Office, 1964), Part I, pp. 2–42. Part II of these hearings took place in
                    February 1965.</p>
            </div>
